# nr-tui-term-os: wire lines for mixdog-term (clipboard, paste attachments and policy, browser opener, native folder picker)

No hot file needs a change. No protocol method, no service, nothing in compose_flip.rs SERVICE_PENDING, no new workspace
dependency edge (the crate already depends on mixdog-fsio, mixdog-js, base64, serde_json; tempfile is a dev-dependency).

## native/core/crates/mixdog-term/Cargo.toml (not a hot file, but not owned by this task: the lead applies it)

[target.'cfg(windows)'.dependencies] `windows`: the folder picker (os.rs `windows_dialog`) calls GetConsoleWindow and creates the
invisible owner window, so two features are added to the list that already holds Win32_System_Com and Win32_UI_Shell:

    windows = { workspace = true, features = ["Win32_System_Com", "Win32_System_Console", "Win32_UI_Shell", "Win32_UI_WindowsAndMessaging"] }

(`Win32_Foundation` comes in through `Win32_UI_Shell`; the `windows` crate version is the one already in Cargo.lock, so the lock
file does not change.)

## What the application task (nr-tui-app) must apply

* Clipboard write: `mixdog_term::clipboard::copy_to_clipboard(&mut terminal_output, text, confirm)`; the first argument is the
  writer the terminal output goes through (the OSC 52 sequence is written to it and flushed). `Ok(CopyOutcome::Terminal)` is
  "OSC 52 only, unconfirmed", `Ok(Copied)` "a native helper confirmed", `Err` carries the message to show.
* Clipboard / path image attach: `paste::read_clipboard_image_attachment(Platform::current(), &SystemRunner, provider, &resize)`
  and `paste::read_image_attachment_from_path(raw, Some(cwd), provider, Platform::current(), &resize)`, where `resize` is a
  closure that calls the core's `thread/resizeImage` with `{ data: <base64 of request.bytes>, mimeType: request.mime_type,
  filename: request.label }` and maps `{ data, mimeType, metadataText }` to `paste::ResizedImage` (an error answer is the
  `Err(message)`). There is no local resize; the size limits and the metadata text are the core's.
* Clipboard text: `paste::read_clipboard_text(Platform::current(), &SystemRunner)`.
* The prompt buffers (use-pasted-buffers.mjs: id sequences, install, snapshot clears) belong to the prompt state of the TUI;
  this crate gives them `format_image_ref`, `format_pasted_text_ref`, `image_reference_ids`, `pasted_text_reference_ids`,
  `build_prompt_content_with_images` (it takes the images as a `BTreeMap<u64, PastedImage>`: ascending ids, as
  `Object.values` iterates them) and `should_fold_pasted_text`.
* Browser: `os::can_open_browser(&os::process_env, Platform::current(), os::is_wsl_host())`, `os::open_in_browser(url)`.
* Folder picker: `os::pick_folder(&os::FolderPickOptions { title, initial_path })` blocks until the dialog is closed (call it
  from a worker thread); `available: false` falls back to typing a path (`reason` names what to install on Linux).
